---
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import SessionsGrid from "../../components/SessionsGrid.astro";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={sessionLabels.plural}
  description={`The twelve-week teaching schedule: what happens in each ${sessionLabels.singular.toLowerCase()}, what to prepare, and what leaves the room.`}
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <p>
    Twelve labs, one for each teaching week, each doing by hand what that
    week's lecture argues for. You bring a catalogue and a calculator; you
    leave with a number you worked out yourself and can defend.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is where the semester's arithmetic actually happens. A lecture can
    establish why a term in the price decomposition matters; the lab is where
    you compute it for a real product on a real shelf, and where a calculation
    that has gone wrong is caught before an assessment comes to depend on it.
    Two of them are fieldwork in an actual outlet, and both carry conduct
    rules — read those before you go.
  </p>
  <p>
    Every lab states a <code>spec</code>: what you should be able to do by the
    time you leave.
  </p>
  <SessionsGrid />
</ContentLayout>
